Pushed a commit on top with the `getLine()` fix from above plus three more from profiling: `ChromeApplier` measures each line once instead of three times, `ArrayLineBuffer` computes its max width lazily, and `resolveStyle()` is memoized per widget keyed on the render revision.

ms/frame, 202x61:

| | full screen, every row changes | sidebar 200 \| main 300, one row |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 8.2 | 3.54 | 2.28 |
| before | 3.50 | 12.88 |
| after | 2.79 | 3.29 |

Note on the style memo: resetting it per frame is not enough, since `renderContainer()` resolves child styles when filtering hidden children, before `beforeRender()` runs, so a class added there would be missed. Keying on the render revision covers it, and `testStyleChangedDuringBeforeRenderIsApplied` guards it.

Suite green (1722 tests), and fuzzing the two commits against each other over 400 random trees x 14 frames gives identical renderer output and screen state.
